# SPA fallback. Client-side routing means /invoices, /approvals etc. exist only
# in the browser — Netlify would otherwise look for a file at that path and 404.
# Status 200 (not 301/302) so the URL in the address bar is preserved and the
# router sees the real path.
#
# Everything in ui/public/ is copied verbatim into dist/ by Vite, which is how
# this reaches Netlify without appearing in the build output.
/*  /index.html  200
